    {
      "id": "claim_fe2e2f58c60d472fad4c9a2fd0475be3",
      "statement": "Interest scoring is a second major subsystem alongside feed polling, built from: an app-owned TypeSafeClient bean defined in config/TypeSafeConfig so the starter's auto-configured bean backs off and a blank API key only disables scoring rather than crashing startup; a jev Resilience4j circuit-breaker+retry pair on integration/JevApiClient(Impl) that is configured and operated independently of the existing raindrop pair; a bounded interestScoringExecutor thread pool (config/InterestScoringConfig) sized by myfeeder.interest.concurrency feeding service/ScoringQueue; and a periodic sweep (scheduler/InterestScoringSweep) that is the only drain loop for scoring work, skipping while Jev is unconfigured, the breaker is open/forced-open, or the app is in cold start.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/config/InterestScoringConfig.java",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:b1f6d879b7f1819a44b5ba28707b7b06ebddba5d574118f8ee168a8f1ccd9e87"
