    {
      "id": "claim_47a6a6b4f9e14812869fb14f0dd0afef",
      "statement": "GET /api/articles/{id}/extracted-content (ArticleController -> ArticleExtractionService) implements a reader-view feature: it loads the article, fetches its original page through the same FeedFetcher used for feed polling (reusing its SSRF guard and size cap), extracts readable content with Readability4J, caches the result on article.extracted_content, and the frontend ReadingPane sanitizes the extracted HTML with DOMPurify using a stricter FORBID_TAGS/FORBID_ATTR:['style'] policy than normal feed content, auto-enabling reader view when the feed provided no content/summary and otherwise offering a manual toggle.",
